Temporary OpenChamber patch for @codemirror/view 6.43.15 (issue #5746).

An iOS keyboard cleaning up dictation inserts a paragraph DIV and keeps writing
into it. CodeMirror reads the paragraph at once and replaces the DIV with its
own line, so the keyboard's later text lands in a detached node and is lost.
The patch reads such a paragraph one frame later, with the rest of its batch,
and keeps the pending change when the editor updates, takes focus or reads
its layout within that frame.

Remove this patch once a @codemirror/view release fixes it upstream. When
bumping @codemirror/view before then, carry it over and rerun
packages/ui/src/components/chat/composer/editor/__tests__/iosNativeParagraph.test.ts.

